INCOHERENT recovery-without-failure .recovery row (line 22): fx-init republished v7 from v5, but v5's last bootlog verdict is 'ok' (fx-init rolls forward only from failed/in-progress)
INCOHERENT bootlog-fabricated-boots 3 in-progress line(s) added but the host started only 2 boot(s) since the previous observation (host boots 2 -> 4) — fx-init writes at most ONE in-progress per boot the host starts (init.zig:4465); the surplus was appended by something that is not fx-init booting
INCOHERENT bootlog-unbound-nonce 2 ADDED .bootlog line(s) carry no nonce the host issued for a boot in this window; first: '5 in-progress 999 deadbad00000001' — the host issued a nonce for EVERY boot of this window (window nonces 2 == delta 2), and fx-init under that regime writes its boot's nonce on every line it appends (init.zig bootlog_append latches the fx.bootnonce= token once per PID1 lifetime), so no boot the host started is behind a nonce-less or foreign-nonce line: this is the forged line-PAIR shape that would otherwise impersonate a silent boot. A line with no nonce field is the PRE-NONCE writer's shape; 'none' is the writer's no-nonce-issued placeholder; a hex nonce from an earlier window or outside the ledger is one this boot was never issued
checks: 6 pass, 2 failed; findings: 3
bound: this seat sees REWRITES and TRUNCATIONS of records it previously observed, cross-record INCOHERENCE, and — anchored on --boots and the per-boot nonce ledger (--nonces) — APPENDED .bootlog/.recovery growth the host cannot account for. IN THE NONCE REGIME (the host issues fx.bootnonce= per boot and every window boot is covered) the forged line-PAIR in a silent boot's slack is CLOSED: every ADDED line must wear a nonce the host issued for a boot in this window, the per-nonce budgets hold at one in-progress / shutdown / .recovery row, the VERDICT accounting is per VERSION — one verdict per in-progress line the window added for that version plus at most one for a version FIRST PUBLISHED in the window (the in-guest activate re-arm, init.zig:3415-3418, which verdicts the activated generation without a new in-progress) — and an unclaimed nonce is REPORTED as a silent boot. What this seat CANNOT see, stated as its bound: a verdict SUBSTITUTED inside a LIVE boot — the agent is root in the guest and can read its own /proc/cmdline nonce, so it can append the verdict itself in the writer's exact shape wearing the live nonce and suppress fx-init's own (a panic before grace expiry); that leaves ONE verdict for one (nonce, version) with every anchor satisfied, and the line's authorship inside the boot that owns the nonce is NOT distinguishable from the host — auditing, not proofing (the defence against substitution is the rollback machinery plus the observation hashes, not this reader); window boots the ledger does not cover (a mixed/manual regime — nonce-less lines are named and counted, but a forged pair in an UNCOVERED boot's slack still passes the arithmetic); boots started off the counting host, or a miscounted / moved --obs-file reuse (the count and the ledger are only as true as the host's own bookkeeping); a coherent tamper on a store first seen at enrollment (the enrollment gap — first run trusts, loudly). That is the honest bound of auditing, not proofing (§6b), printed on every run so the tool never implies more than it knows.
evidence: the store's own records only — attempts.jsonl (the harness self-report) is never opened.
VERDICT: incoherent (3 finding(s))
